  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q15-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "15",
    "prompt": "Consider $\\triangle ABC$ for which $b=5$, $c=8$ and $\\angle A=60^\\circ$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p33-q15-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Show that the third side of this triangle is also an integer.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$a=7$, so the third side is also an integer.",
          "worked": "By the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}a^2&=b^2+c^2-2bc\\cos A\\\\a^2&=5^2+8^2-2(5)(8)\\cos60^\\circ\\\\a^2&=25+64-40\\\\a^2&=49\\\\a&=7.\\end{align*}$$\nAll three side lengths are integers.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      },
      {
        "id": "p33-q15-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p33-q15-b-setup",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "In fact, there are infinitely many triangles with integer side lengths and one angle equal to ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "60^\\circ",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ". To show this, let ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "m",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "n",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " be any positive integers (where ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "m>n",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ") and consider ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\triangle ABC",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " for which",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p33-q15-b-equations",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "center",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\begin{aligned}a&=m^2-mn+n^2\\\\b&=2mn-n^2\\\\c&=m^2-n^2.\\end{aligned}",
                  "display": true
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "id": "p33-q15-b-task",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 1,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Show that ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\angle A=60^\\circ",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ".",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p33-q15-b-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\angle A=60^\\circ",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p33-q15-b-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Substitution gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "b^2+c^2-a^2=bc",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ", so the cosine rule gives ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\cos A=\\frac12",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Substituting the side lengths gives\n$$\\begin{align*}b^2+c^2-a^2&=(2mn-n^2)^2+(m^2-n^2)^2-(m^2-mn+n^2)^2\\\\b^2+c^2-a^2&=2m^3n-m^2n^2-2mn^3+n^4\\\\b^2+c^2-a^2&=n(2m-n)(m^2-n^2)\\\\b^2+c^2-a^2&=bc.\\end{align*}$$\nBy the cosine rule,\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos A&=\\frac{b^2+c^2-a^2}{2bc}\\\\\\cos A&=\\frac{bc}{2bc}\\\\\\cos A&=\\frac12\\\\A&=60^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 57
      }
    ]
  },
